MID_LGV_2_M02_Bel_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Bel_m01_001: It is innocent people who feel most deeply the\nravages of war. I have seen that.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Bel_m01_002: And it's why, as best I can, I will stop unreasonable\nsuffering. That is my mission as king.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Bel_m01: <BLN>That is my mission.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Seo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Seo_m01_001: Our supplies are ample, but not inexhaustible.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Seo_m01_002: And we cannot rely on Fort Zanbar forever. In the\nend, our only chance for survival is to march on.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Seo_m01: <BLN>We can only march on.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Tia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Tia_m01_001: Since my grandfather was a strategist for Arago, a lot\nof what I know is Aragonian.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Tia_m01_002: I need to be careful that no one suspects me of being\na spy. We don't need any strife like that.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Tia_m01: <BLN>I need to be careful!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Pet_m01_001: It looks like all the nations are getting involved in the\nfight. There's tons of knights around.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Pet_m01_002: I'm not too sure what kind of salute I should be\ngiving anybody though. Hmm...
MID_LGA_2_M02_Pet_m01: <BLN>I'm not sure...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Hur_m01_001: The empire used more tools than simple faith to\nmaintain control...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Hur_m01_002: The strength of their fortifications, the military might\nof the temples, the power of the gods themselves...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Hur_m01_003: Now that we're fighting them, I realize I've never\nfully understood their true strength.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Hur_m01: <BLN>The power of the gods themselves...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Max_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Max_m01_001: If war's good for anything, it's bringing out people's\ntrue natures.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Max_m01_002: Same old scene, again and again. Even I'm sick of it.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Max_m01_003: Wonder if there's some way to change it.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Max_m01: <BLN>War...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Gol_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Gol_m01_001: I got teary-eyed seeing Brezarant's army charge\ninto battle behind their king.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Gol_m01_002: From a general to a gladiator to a king...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Gol_m01_003: WAAAH! My brother's the best, and always\nhas been!
MID_LGA_2_M02_Gol_m01: <BLN>It put a tear in my eye!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Gat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Gat_m01_001: Hmm. The war has begun, and our king has made\nwhat may prove to be a dangerous alliance.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Gat_m01_002: Still, I see only a leader moving straight forward with\nhis integrity unclouded.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Gat_m01_003: Which means I was correct in my estimation.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Gat_m01: <BLN>I was not wrong.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Dan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Dan_m01_001: The battle at the Klytius plains, a dialogue between\nmonarchs, the formation of a new alliance...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Dan_m01_002: I never thought I would pay witness to events of such\nhistoric importance!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Dan_m01_003: It's all even more fascinating than I'd hoped.\nThank the gods I came along!
MID_LGA_2_M02_Dan_m01: <BLN>It's the stuff of drama!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Fab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Fab_m01_001: The beasts are at it again—playing their games of\nstate and starting a war.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Fab_m01_002: In the past I would have watched from the sidelines,\nfilled with grim displeasure.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Fab_m01_003: Yet now I come to your aid and intervene directly.\nYou should thank me.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Fab_m01: <BLN>I offer my aid.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Esm_m01_001: The other day a soldier said to me, "You're so strong!"\nFeels strange.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Esm_m01_002: I don't know that I want to be recognized for my skill\nduring a war. I don't like it.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Esm_m01_003: Really, I want to use my strength on the seas.\nNothing wrong with being strong at fishing.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Esm_m01: <BLN>Feels strange.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Urs_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Urs_m01_001: Pious soldiers always make me uncomfortable. I've\nhad more than a few poor experiences with them...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Urs_m01_002: But I know in my gut that, deep down, they're\nregular people, just like me.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Urs_m01_003: Perhaps they are also thinking they don't wish to\nbecome a beast.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Urs_m01: <BLN>I have mixed feelings.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Sim_m01_001: It must be a lot of pressure, fighting with the weight\nof your ancestors behind you...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Sim_m01_002: Can't relate. Dying for family, or gods, or whatever,\ndoesn't matter. Once you die, you've already lost.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Sim_m01_003: So I'll win this war. And when I'm done here, I'll\nmove on to the next, then the next...
MID_LGA_2_M02_Sim_m01: <BLN>I'll win this.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Lou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Lou_m01_001: Merchants who say things like "war is money" give\nthe rest of us a bad name.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Lou_m01_002: Good business is about unity, really. We shouldn't\nrelish in pain just because it's easy coin!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Lou_m01_003: I'm glad selling death as a way to get rich isn't the\ntrading company's attitude.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Lou_m01: <BLN>Those kinds of merchants...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Fia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Fia_m01_001: Every time I heal a soldier's wounds, they thank me...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Fia_m01_002: But is it right to heal their old scars just to send them\nback to the battlefield for new ones?
MID_LGV_2_M02_Fia_m01_003: I don't know... But either way, we can't afford to lose.\nIf healing's all I can do, so be it.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Fia_m01: <BLN>I will do all I can.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Die_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Die_m01_001: I surveyed the situation from hiding. I confirmed\nthat the fort's defenses are as strong as we thought.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Die_m01_002: In the end, we'll need to face the enemy head-on.\nNo matter what our foes throw at us.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Die_m01: <BLN>I surveyed the situation...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Lor_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Lor_m01_001: If we lose this war, I'd guess that Brezarant will get\nreally messed up.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Lor_m01_002: And if that happens...Credna's temple is done\nfor. And Ozin with it!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Lor_m01_003: I've gotta do what I can to stop all this. Good thing\nI'm trained up in how to use weapons.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Lor_m01: <BLN>I'll stop it! I've got to!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Set_m01_001: You can rely on me to the fullest. I may be an\noutsider here, but I welcome being of use.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Set_m01_002: I mastered the art of war long ago. Have no fear.\nI can be useful in ways you wouldn't imagine.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Set_m01: <BLN>Rely on me to the fullest.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Nin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Nin_m01_001: The spirits are scared... The flames of war are\nbreaking out across the land. I am also uneasy...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Nin_m01_002: Or is it that the spirits are trying to tell me...that\nwe're being drawn into a vortex of no escape...
MID_LGA_2_M02_Nin_m01: <BLN>The spirits are scared.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Bon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Bon_m01_001: I am concerned about the morale of our soldiers.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Bon_m01_002: The arrival of the Brezarant reinforcements cheered\nthem, but if our supplies dwindle, the mood will shift.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Bon_m01_003: If they began to rebel, our alliance would crumble\nfrom within. We must take pains to avoid this.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Bon_m01: <BLN>I worry for our soldiers...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Tob_m01_001: From fightin' in the open to taking a stronghold, no\nmatter what the objective is, our job is the same.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Tob_m01_002: Just like the War of Grania, I'll smash through their\ndefenses with one blow!
MID_LGA_2_M02_Tob_m01: <BLN>I'll smash my way in!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Lil_m01_001: The more I think about Agris Stronghold, the worse\nit seems. I'm gonna need a serious raise for this.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Lil_m01_002: Though money won't do me any good if I don't make\nit out alive. Victory first, cash later.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Lil_m01: <BLN>I'm gonna need a serious raise.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Lys_m01_001: It's been gratifying to interact so freely with the\nknights of Brezarant.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Lys_m01_002: I find their political insights well considered. I'll need\nto report them back to my uncle.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Lys_m01: <BLN>It's a grand learning opportunity.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Buc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Buc_m01_001: I was surprised to see the army in such good spirits.\nQueen Theodora is an impressive unifier of people.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Buc_m01_004: I was impressed to see the army in such good\nspirits—but they had a unifying leader.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Buc_m01_002: Bertrand as well. How he came to take Brezarant's\nthrone, I can hardly fathom.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Buc_m01_005: Two of them, I should say. The path from prisoner\nto king of Brezarant, I can hardly imagine...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Buc_m01_003: Then again, as I'm constantly, painfully reminded,\nmany things in this world are beyond my ken.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Buc_m01_006: Then again, as I'm constantly reminded, many things\nin this world are beyond my ken.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Buc_m01: <BLN>Many things are beyond my ken.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Sci_m01_001: You know, this camp's not exactly lacking for\ngorgeous women.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Sci_m01_002: Heh heh. Put me in the worst fight I've ever seen,\nand the sight of a beauty will still cheer me up.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Sci_m01_003: I want to be on the vanguard in our next battle,\nthat I might make their hearts flutter!
MID_LGA_2_M02_Sci_m01: <BLN>Look at them all!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Moo_m01_001: Let's see. I need to prepare the medicine, help schlep\nthe supplies...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Moo_m01_002: There's so much for me to do between battles.\nBut the others need it!
MID_LGA_2_M02_Moo_m01: <BLN>Got to support everyone!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Mic_m01_001: When I was a mercenary, I fought anywhere and\neverywhere. Fields, mountains, deserts, you name it.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Mic_m01_002: Saramis and Brezarant's soldiers are skilled, I'll give\nthem that, but they lack that kind of experience.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Mic_m01_003: I guess it's up to me to train them, isn't it? I'll make\nsure they live up to their potential.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Mic_m01: <BLN>It's up to me.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Oly_m01_001: Once, baffled by my father's opinion, I asked Kalla\nwhat she thought of it.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Oly_m01_002: "I don't understand either," she said. I assumed she\nwas comforting me...but perhaps it was the truth?
MID_LGA_2_M02_Oly_m01: <BLN>Was she actually telling the truth?
MID_LGV_2_M02_Naz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Naz_m01_001: The empire sure does like their walls and gates,\ndon't they?
MID_LGV_2_M02_Naz_m01_002: Well, we're gonna break through that stronghold and\nkeep on going! There's no stopping us now!
MID_LGA_2_M02_Naz_m01: <BLN>There's no stopping us!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Sar_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Sar_m01_001: We won the opening battle, but so many were hurt.\nI did what I could, provided healing magic.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Sar_m01_002: If we're going to win this war, we have to help one\nanother survive.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Sar_m01: <BLN>We can survive this.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Dai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Dai_m01_001: I know war costs money, but I don't really get why.\nI guess moving this many people ain't cheap.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Dai_m01_002: Anyway, I'm gonna go hunt in the mountains! I at\nleast want to cover what it costs to feed me!
MID_LGA_2_M02_Dai_m01: <BLN>I don't get why.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Hal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Hal_m01_001: I performed some tricks in the campground, and\nit went really well! Everyone seemed to like it.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Hal_m01_002: I hope I helped them forget how tough life is for\na little while.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Hal_m01: <BLN>That went well!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Guj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Guj_m01_001: Some mercenaries will do anything for money.\nBut that's an incredible mistake.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Guj_m01_002: You put your life on the line when you sign up for\nfighting. That includes even me.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Guj_m01_003: That's why I never choose battles for money. I'll\nfight only where I think I can survive.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Guj_m01: <BLN>I don't go where the money is.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Yan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Yan_m01_001: The gods are cowardly. That fortress, which blocks\nthe Saramis advance, was placed here long ago.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Yan_m01_002: Imagine! The gods, for all their power and posturing,\nactually feared the children of Damascar.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Yan_m01_003: It's a relief, actually. I've always thought that the\ngods fear humans. The fortress proves that.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Yan_m01: <BLN>It's a relief, actually.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Iio_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Iio_m01_001: Of course Arago would side with the Dagdan Empire.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Iio_m01_002: Still, though it's no surprise, it grieves me.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Iio_m01_003: Arago no longer has the will to join the rebellion\nas Brezarant did.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Iio_m01: <BLN>Was I expecting this?
MID_LGV_2_M02_Pep_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Pep_m01_001: Saramis and Brezarant have now, in name and\nactuality, seceded from the empire.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Pep_m01_002: The Dagdan system of life that has long centered\non the temples is threatened.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Pep_m01_003: And we? Ah, well, WE have sworn to support\nthe Alliance, knowing it is fully righteous!
MID_LGA_2_M02_Pep_m01: <BLN>We are sure of our course.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Noc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Noc_m01_001: I'm from Brezarant, you know. I always wondered\nwhy we hadn't had a king for a long time.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Noc_m01_002: Then I heard that the White-Maned Demon had\nclaimed the throne! I was actually pretty happy!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Noc_m01_003: I have no complaints about such a king. Besides, I'd\nlove a chance at a royal sparring match!
MID_LGA_2_M02_Noc_m01: <BLN>I was happy to hear it...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Sop_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Sop_m01_001: I'd had my eye on a very tasty place to eat for a\nwhile. But with the war, I can forget about all that.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Sop_m01_002: I'd been hoping to treat Anna too, after the Heroic\nGames ended.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Sop_m01_003: There's no point in regretting it. I'll just try to find\nan even better place to eat somewhere else!
MID_LGA_2_M02_Sop_m01: <BLN>So frustrating!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Cat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Cat_m01_001: What a world... A skilled artisan that I've long\nsupported has died.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Cat_m01_002: And there were already so few who could make\nthings I desired at a sterling level of quality.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Cat_m01_003: We must stop this cruel war as fast as we can.\nI must have quality objects to ease my feelings!
MID_LGA_2_M02_Cat_m01: <BLN>Such tragedy!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Ned_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Ned_m01_001: I was concerned about some soldiers I used to\nknow long ago. So I went to visit them.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Ned_m01_002: I was surprised that they gave me such a warm\nreception. They said I gave them strength to fight.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Ned_m01_003: It's hard for me to understand. Maybe they're so\nworried that they take comfort in old comrades.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Ned_m01: <BLN>I got a warm reception, but...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Zac_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Zac_m01_001: Haaa ha! The battles ahead will surely leave\ncorpses aplenty!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Zac_m01_002: The dead don't care if I search their pockets.\nSo, time to rake in some gold!
MID_LGA_2_M02_Zac_m01: <BLN>Gold, gold, gold!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Maj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Maj_m01_001: What a bunch of mopey people. Pathetic!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Maj_m01_002: You gotta be ready to go even when you're just\nsittin' around. Yeah, be ready to FIGHT!
MID_LGA_2_M02_Maj_m01: <BLN>Pathetic!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Ven_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Ven_m01_001: Rookie soldiers don't know how to speak to a\nveteran like me! Especially when they're drinking!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Ven_m01_002: One of them told me I deserve to live out my final\ndays in peace. How dare he?! I'm still fighting fit!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Ven_m01_003: I'll decide when I deserve to take it easy, not them!\nWhat nerve!
MID_LGA_2_M02_Ven_m01: <BLN>I'm still fighting fit!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Ini_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Ini_m01_001: I wonder if Mom and Dad are OK. It's been too\nlong since I've seen them...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Ini_m01_002: I feel uneasy leaving them on their own for such a\nlong time. But I have faith they'll be alright.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Ini_m01: <BLN>I hope they're OK...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Jas_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Jas_m01_001: I like to use my super-secret strategy in battle,\nbut it's hard to know where exactly to use it!
MID_LGV_2_M02_Jas_m01_002: It's silly to use it just for the sake of it, but sillier\nnot to use it at all.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Jas_m01: <BLN>It's always difficult.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Ale_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Ale_m01_001: A shortage of provisions... Couldn't we work\nsomething out with Jurah's temple?
MID_LGV_2_M02_Ale_m01_002: No, that won't do. That'd put Jurah herself into a\ndangerous position.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Ale_m01_003: And I wouldn't dare ask her myself. I've betrayed\nthe Divine Emperor. I can't bring her more trouble.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Ale_m01: <BLN>A shortage of provisions...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Cen_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Cen_m01_001: Saramis and Brezarant have won their first victory\nagainst the empire.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Cen_m01_002: That victory will be fleeting. Now the true struggle\nwill begin.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Cen_m01_003: Aurora cares so for the people of these nations. \nI pray the fires of war don't spread far.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Cen_m01: <BLN>Saramis and Brezarant...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Kir_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Kir_m01_001: Many pirates on the Danann Sea are descendants\nof the kingdom of Damascar.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Kir_m01_002: Now, Dagda's latest outburst could scare up even\nmore people like that.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Kir_m01_003: If I was still leading the Black-Swan Pirates, I'd\nrecruit any folks with nowhere to go!
MID_LGA_2_M02_Kir_m01: <BLN>The pirates of the Danann Sea...
MID_LGV_2_M02_Nuz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_Nuz_m01_001: Some soldiers of the empire, Brezarant, and even\nSaramis show curiosity and fear toward the Har Hali.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Nuz_m01_002: But we are no less proud for it. We've never minded\nbeing the object of strange looks from our allies.
MID_LGV_2_M02_Nuz_m01_003: And if our enemies fear us, then we will take full\nadvantage of their terror.
MID_LGA_2_M02_Nuz_m01: <BLN>We will prey on their fear.
MID_LGV_2_M02_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_B01_m01_001: Honestly, part of me was relieved when they recalled\nthose of us in the cavalry.
MID_LGV_2_M02_B01_m01_002: It doesn't feel good to confiscate everything from\nordinary people as they wail in despair.
MID_LGA_2_M02_B01_m01: <BLN>It's a relief, really.
MID_LGV_2_M02_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_B02_m01_001: I am afraid the king may be about to learn a lesson\nin the way of the world.
MID_LGV_2_M02_B02_m01_002: Playing the waiting game will end in our deaths.\nWhat happened at Damascar proved that.
MID_LGV_2_M02_B02_m01_003: Pillaging is something people in our situation have to\ndo to maintain an army capable of resisting.
MID_LGV_2_M02_B02_m01_004: If Her Majesty orders it, I'll go along with it. But how\nlong will we last clinging to these naïve ideas?
MID_LGA_2_M02_B02_m01: <BLN>This isn't how the world works.
MID_LGV_2_M02_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_B03_m01_001: We have made enemies of the gods. But we're no\nstranger to victory against daunting odds.
MID_LGV_2_M02_B03_m01_002: True, our usual foes are human, but their ways are so\nunlike ours that they may as well be gods.
MID_LGV_2_M02_B03_m01_003: So there's no need to be afraid of the coming battle.\nIf I think of it that way, maybe I can pull through.
MID_LGA_2_M02_B03_m01: <BLN>There's no need to be afraid.
MID_LGV_2_M02_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_B04_m01_001: Bravery is the hallmark of a Brezarant soldier.\nCowardice and hesitation have no place in combat.
MID_LGV_2_M02_B04_m01_002: Emotion is the enemy of technique. To show fear on\nthe battlefield is to invite your own death.
MID_LGA_2_M02_B04_m01: <BLN>There's no room for hesitation!
MID_LGV_2_M02_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_B05_m01_001: This is the Saraminian headquarters, where the\ndeath-worshipping children of Damascar camp...
MID_LGV_2_M02_B05_m01_002: I've had no complaints about them as comrades.\nI just find them kind of creepy.
MID_LGA_2_M02_B05_m01: <BLN>The Saraminian headquarters...
MID_LGV_2_M02_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M02_B06_m01_001: Morale is higher than ever. From new recruits to\nveterans, the army adores their king. 
MID_LGV_2_M02_B06_m01_002: If the sentiment holds, we might not even have any\ndeserters. I hate having to punish people on my side.
MID_LGA_2_M02_B06_m01: <BLN>The army's morale is high.